from pathlib import Path
import html,json
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;P=R.parent
load=lambda p:json.loads(p.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
q=load(R/'QUALIFICATION.json');e=lambda x:html.escape(str(x))
def table(h,rs):return '<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+e(x)+'</th>' for x in h)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+str(x)+'</td>' for x in r)+'</tr>' for r in rs)+'</tbody></table></div>'
body='<p class="muted">VOYNICH · CORRECTION QUALIFICATION · v77</p><h1>Resolve the opening-search precision limit</h1><p class="notice"><strong>Qualification: '+q['status']+'.</strong> Numerical correction controls were completed before manuscript score access. The old v75 pooled-tail precision failure is preserved; this is a separately frozen maxT method, not a relabelled v75 p-value.</p>'
body+='<h2>Frozen method</h2><p>Each signed count contrast is centred by its pooled observed+shuffle mean and divided by √(pooled variance + 1 count²). Each row’s largest absolute standardized contrast across the entire original opening family supplies the null maximum. The target is compared directly with those maxima, instead of separately ranking thousands of tiny tail probabilities. No normal-distribution tail approximation is used.</p><p>The one-count regularizer is fixed at the integer count scale and keeps rare or constant contrasts from producing unbounded standardization. It changes the relative weighting of the search family; this is an explicitly different multiplicity statistic. Every original candidate is retained. Mean and scale are symmetric across rows, preserving the finite exchangeable-row ranking argument.</p><p>All 14 original H/F hand/section/Currier/rawP panels and the Bonferroni factor14 are unchanged. No hands/readings are pooled, and no extra manuscript shuffles or narrower candidate search are introduced.</p>'
body+='<h2>Qualification before rescore</h2><p>Eight independently seeded anonymous joint-score banks used all 14 actual family dimensions, 4,096 exchangeable integer rows per panel, correlated columns, unequal count scales, position-only mean shifts, rare one-count events and constants. These are numerical controls, not known historical texts or semantic-role validation.</p>'
body+=table(['Bank','Global null flags / 4096 rotations','Lowest–highest attainable adjusted p','Worst panel 8-SD detections / 64','H-only false paired maximum / 64','All gates'],[[b['bank'],str(b['global_null_flags'])+'/4096',f'{min(b["minimum_achievable_panel_adjusted_p"]):.5f}–{max(b["minimum_achievable_panel_adjusted_p"]):.5f}',str(min(x['detections']['8'] for x in b['dose_results']))+'/64',str(max(x['false_both_pass'] for x in b['H_only_paired_controls']))+'/64','PASS' if b['passes'] else 'FAIL'] for b in q['banks']])
body+='<p>Null rotations are dependent pseudo-observations of each bank. Their count checks the finite-row rank bound, not 4,096 independent empirical false-positive trials. Global flags must be ≤floor(.05×4096). Minimum attainable adjusted p must be ≤.01 in every panel. Strong 8-null-SD plants must achieve ≥90% detection in every bank/panel; moderate dose power is recorded without a pass requirement. H-only plants must not create >5% false both-reading conclusions.</p>'
body+='<details><summary>Every dose and every failed planted example count</summary>'+table(['Bank','Panel shape','2 SD /64','4 SD /64','6 SD /64','8 SD /64'],[[b['bank'],str(x['panel_index'])+' · '+str(x['shape_columns'])+' contrasts',x['detections']['2'],x['detections']['4'],x['detections']['6'],x['detections']['8']] for b in q['banks'] for x in b['dose_results']])+'</details><p>The same bank is reused across planted rows/doses; those power trials are dependent. A complete small authored line-permutation orbit separately verified the unchanged encoder’s overlapping-class counts, unknown barriers and direct maxT tails. It is too small to qualify 14-panel precision by itself.</p>'
if q['status']=='PASS' and (R/'RESULTS.json').exists():
 d=load(R/'RESULTS.json');old=load(P/'opening-order-audit-v75/RESULTS.json')
 body+='<h2>Rescore after qualification · sh- → qok-</h2>'
 body+=table(['Section','Hand','Variety','Reading','Forward / reverse','D','Regularized Z','Null-max exceedances /4999','Family p','All-panel p'],[[e(p['section']),e(p['hand']),p['variety'],p['reading'],str(p['rules'][0]['forward'])+'/'+str(p['rules'][0]['reverse']),p['rules'][0]['observed_D'],f'{p["rules"][0]["observed_Z"]:.3f}',p['rules'][0]['max_tail_exceedances'],f'{p["rules"][0]["p_family"]:.4f}',f'{p["rules"][0]["p_all_panels"]:.4f}'] for p in d['panels']])
 groups={}
 for p in d['panels']:groups.setdefault((p['section'],p['hand'],p['variety'],p['format']),{})[p['reading']]=p
 both=[]
 for key,reads in groups.items():
  if set(reads)=={'H','F'} and all(v['rules'][0]['observed_Z']>0 and v['rules'][0]['p_all_panels']<=.05 for v in reads.values()):both.append(' / '.join(key))
 body+='<p class="notice"><strong>Positive principal direction passing the full screen in both readings:</strong> '+e('; '.join(both) or 'none')+'. A hand label containing a comma is ambiguous and cannot establish another known scribe. H/F agreement is correspondence between readings, not independent manuscript replication.</p>'
 body+='<p>The same saved v75 score matrices were rescored only after PASS. Word counts, source loci, prefixes, support filters, endpoint/unknown-preserving within-line null and every reverse-order exception are unchanged. New mean/scale/max arrays and all target calculations are saved for replay.</p>'
 body+='<details><summary>Other originally reported relations and all nonpassing outcomes</summary>'
 for p in d['panels']:body+='<h3>'+e(p['section']+' · '+p['hand']+' · '+p['variety']+' · '+p['reading'])+'</h3>'+table(['A → B','Forward / reverse','D','Z','Family p','All-panel p'],[[e(x['A']+' → '+x['B']),str(x['forward'])+'/'+str(x['reverse']),x['observed_D'],f'{x["observed_Z"]:.3f}',f'{x["p_family"]:.4f}',f'{x["p_all_panels"]:.4f}'] for x in p['rules']])
 body+='</details><details><summary>Zero/negative folios and every reverse principal source pair</summary>'
 for p,s in zip(d['panels'],old['source_events']):
  body+='<h3>'+e(p['section']+' · '+p['hand']+' · '+p['reading'])+'</h3>'+table(['Folio','Forward','Reverse','D'],[[e(f),v['forward'],v['reverse'],v['forward']-v['reverse']] for f,v in s['folios'].items()])
  for ev in s['events']:
   if ev['orientation']!='reverse':continue
   i=ev['ordinal']-1;body+='<article><p>'+e(ev['locator'])+' · ordinal '+str(ev['ordinal'])+'</p><p class="raw">'+' '.join('□' if w is None else '<mark>'+e(w)+'</mark>' if j in (i,i+1) else e(w) for j,w in enumerate(ev['tokens']))+'</p></article>'
 body+='</details><p><a href="MC-PRECISION.json">Finite-shuffle precision estimates</a> are explicitly approximate because pooled centering/scaling couples rows; they are not exact independent-binomial confidence intervals.</p>'
else:body+='<p class="notice">Qualification failed or rescore absent. Manuscript scores were not opened by the guarded rescore. Preserve all failed gates; no tuned rerun is substituted.</p>'
body+='<h2>Scope of the conclusion</h2><p>Passing numerical qualification resolves the specific finite-rank search-correction problem. It does not validate every assumption of the line-shuffle null. That null preserves each line’s words, endpoints and unknown barriers, but not exact interior ordinals or every possible word-boundary mechanism. No meanings, grammatical word classes, semantic operations or biological analogies are inferred.</p><p><a href="QUALIFICATION.json">All qualification gates and failures</a> · <a href="EXACT-ORBIT.json">Authored exact-orbit check</a> · <a href="PROTOCOL.json">Pre-control frozen protocol</a> · <a href="FREEZE.json">Input/script hashes</a> · <a href="RESULTS.json">Rescore if qualified</a> · <a href="VERIFICATION.json">Verification</a> · <a href="../opening-order-audit-v75/report.html">Preserved v75 failure</a></p><p>Browser visual review not performed. Source and numerical checks are separate from appearance.</p>'
css='''<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark;--bg:light-dark(#f5f2e9,#18251f);--fg:light-dark(#203f35,#e2e9df);--sub:light-dark(#54695b,#b4c7b7);--rule:light-dark(#c0ccbd,#48604d);--fill:light-dark(#e5ebda,#2a3e2d);--mark:light-dark(#e6edb7,#526330)}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:16px/1.55 system-ui}main{max-width:1450px;padding:30px;margin:auto}h1{font-size:32px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:23px;margin-top:30px}p{max-width:1100px}a{color:inherit}.muted{color:var(--sub)}.notice{padding:16px;background:var(--fill)}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:9px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}.raw{font:15px/1.8 ui-monospace,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere}mark{background:var(--mark);color:inherit}article{border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}summary{cursor:pointer}details{margin:16px 0}@media(max-width:700px){main{padding:16px}}</style>'''
(R/'report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Opening-order correction qualification · v77</title>'+css+'</head><body><main>'+body+'</main></body></html>',encoding='utf-8');print('Qualification report written.')
